  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Define a **block** of a binary string to be a maximal substring consisting of the same character. For example, the blocks of 1100100\\text{1100100}1100100 are 11\\text{11}11, 00\\text{00}00, 1\\text{1}1 and 00\\text{00}00.\n\nYou are given a string SSS, of size NNN, consisting of characters 000, 111 or ???. It is guaranteed that SSS does not begin or end with a ???, i.e. S1≠?S_1 \\ne ?S1​=? and SN≠?S_N \\ne ?SN​=?.\n\nYour job is to replace each ??? with either 000 or 111, and then obtain a binary string with exactly KKK ones. Among all valid strings with exactly KKK ones, find the **minimum number of blocks possible**.\n\nYou must solve the above problem for each K=0,1,2,…,NK = 0, 1, 2, \\ldots, NK=0,1,2,…,N. For certain KKK, it may be impossible and you should print −1-1−1 instead.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line contains a single integer NNN - the size of the string SSS.\nThe second line contains a string SSS.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line N+1N + 1N+1 integers, the answers for K=0,1,2,…,NK = 0, 1, 2, \\ldots, NK=0,1,2,…,N.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "3≤N≤2⋅1053 \\le N \\le 2 \\cdot 10^53≤N≤2⋅105",
      "Si∈{0,1,?}S_i \\in \\{0, 1, ?\\}Si​∈{0,1,?}",
      "S1≠?S_1 \\ne ?S1​=?, SN≠?S_N \\ne ?SN​=?",
      "∣S∣=N|S| = N∣S∣=N",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n3\n0?0\n5\n0?1?1\n7\n1100100\n5\n0???0",
        "output": "1 3 -1 -1\n-1 -1 4 2 2 -1\n-1 -1 -1 4 -1 -1 -1 -1\n1 3 3 3 -1 -1",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1 : It is impossible to have K=2K = 2K=2 or K=3K = 3K=3 because there is only 111 ??? to replace and no already filled 111.\nFor K=0K = 0K=0, the only string is 000000000 which has 111 block.\nFor K=1K = 1K=1, the only string is 010010010 which has 333 blocks."
      }
    ]
